{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAp8uerV8Jg3fPSN8exP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The cause is `Disallow: /v1/` in `site/robots.txt`, which was added on 2026-09-07. I changed `site/robots.txt` to fix it, but I haven't deployed it or tested it against Google. I did check the new rules with a small longest-match script, and each path came out as intended.\n\n**Why the pages are soft 404s.** Each note page is an HTML shell that `app.js` fills by fetching `/v1/notes/{slug}`. Googlebot follows robots.txt when it renders, so it can't make that fetch. `app.js` then shows its \"NOT FOUND\" screen on a page that still returns HTTP 200, which Google classes as a soft 404. Browsers and curl load the data fine.\n\nThe Search Console files back this up:\n- The live test for `/n/drip-line-pressure` shows a successful HTTP 200 fetch but rendered text of \"NOT FOUND\".\n- The four notes crawled in October are Soft 404, while the two notes crawled in August, before the robots change, are still Indexed.\n\n**The fix.** I kept the general block and added an exception for the public read endpoints:\n```\nDisallow: /v1/\nDisallow: /admin/\nAllow: /v1/notes\nDisallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions\n```\nGoogle uses the longest matching rule. That opens `/v1/notes` and `/v1/notes/{slug}`. The reactions path, `/v1/me*`, `/v1/auth/*` and `/admin/` stay blocked.\n\n**What you need to do:**\n1. Deploy the file and check it with `curl -s https://fieldnotes.example/robots.txt`.\n2. In Search Console, request a robots.txt recrawl.\n3. Run \"Test live URL\" on `/n/drip-line-pressure`, then request indexing.\n\n`ANSWER.md` has the cause, the fix and which parts of your colleague's note applied. Their robots.txt diagnosis, the Allow plus longer-Disallow fix and the longest-match testing all applied. Their `/v1/stories` routes became `/v1/notes` here. I didn't do their step of writing plain links into the served HTML, because this repo has no build step. I left that, and making `app.js` show \"not found\" only on a real 404, as optional follow-ups."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1227,"cache_read_input_tokens":25446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1227},"output_tokens":751,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a6edad7-3137-4e84-89d2-cdd40a4e4c67","uuid":"8f7a46fd-2500-47fb-84b7-bbe0c5c32add","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:33:27.093Z","request_id":"req_011CgAp8uNVEmeo5qHoxqhm9"}
